# Agent — repository ignore rules
#
# This is a *workspace* repository: it holds the AgentOrg engine, the native console, and the skill
# discovery links. The rules below separate what is source (reviewed, diffable, committed) from what is
# generated, personal, or secret.
#
# AgentOrg/ has its own .gitignore for its own concerns. This file covers the workspace root, where the
# extra directories live.

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Live keys never enter the repository. `credentials.example.json` is the committed template; the real
# `credentials.json` stays local, which is why a key pasted into the console is not committed with it.
credentials.json
*.env
*.key
*.pem

# ── Agent runtime state — not project source ─────────────────────────────────
# `.reasonix/` holds this agent's own session state: per-task snapshots, event logs, locks, and
# clipboard attachments from a session. It is working state that happens to live in the tree, not
# something a reviewer would ever want in a diff — and it changes on every run, so committing it would
# mean a commit per session that says nothing.
.reasonix/

# The engine's own run state, when a project workspace is rooted at the repo.
.agent_state/
.agent-run/
telemetry/
projects/

# A roster and authored skills are personal working state, not shared source.
.agentorg/

# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SwiftPM's artifact directory. `AgentOrg/macos/.build/` is ignored by AgentOrg's own rules; this
# catches a stray one at the package root, which is where SwiftPM puts it when invoked from there.
.build/
macos/.build/
macos/.swiftpm/
*.xcodeproj
*.xcworkspace
DerivedData/

# ── Language runtimes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# ── Skill discovery links ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `scripts/init-project.sh` creates these as symlinks into the Skills library. They are absolute paths
# on one machine, so committing them would hand every other checkout a broken link — the links are
# derived, and the script that makes them is committed instead.
.agents/skills
.claude/skills
.copilot/skills
.github/skills
.cursor/skills
.codex/skills
.gemini/skills
.windsurf/skills
.cline/skills
.opencode/skills

# ── OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
